@@ -100,19 +100,30 @@ Each pet is recorded against exactly one owner, with a name, a birth date, and a
 
 ### Visits
 
-<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a>
+<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a><a id="req-visitedit-001"></a>
 
 A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`.
 
+A booked visit can be corrected afterwards. A correction replaces its date and its description, and the correction form opens on the values that visit holds today `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]`. A correction meets the same rules as a booking, and it lands on the visit that already exists rather than adding a second one. A correction is reached by its own address; nothing on the owner's record points at it yet.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a pet, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then the visit is recorded and the booking is confirmed.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a blank description, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the description is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the date is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-002]` given a pet with earlier visits, when a new visit is being booked, then those earlier visits are shown with their dates and descriptions.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when its correction form is opened, then the form shows that visit's current date and description.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a description and a date later than today, when the correction is submitted, then that visit carries the new values and the owner's record is shown.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given an accepted correction, when the pet's visits are counted, then the count is unchanged and no second visit exists.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a blank description, when the correction is submitted, then the correction is refused and the description is named.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the correction is submitted, then the correction is refused and the date is named.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
+3. Correcting a visit that is not the named pet's is refused, as booking against another owner's pet is.
+4. The future-date rule holds for a correction too, so a visit whose date has passed cannot keep that date.
+
+**ADR:** [ADR: Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling Stays Out](adr/2026-08-18-non-goal-visit-correction.md)
 
